# .env.s3 — credentials and switches for the direct-to-S3 ingest variant.
#
# Kept separate from .env on purpose: .env holds the credentials the whole
# testbed depends on, and regenerating it rotates every secret. Nothing here is
# needed by the default topology, so this file can be created, edited or
# deleted without touching a working testbed.
#
# Consumed via `env_file:` in docker-compose.yml (minio, minio-init,
# cvmfs-prepub) rather than ${VAR} interpolation — compose only interpolates
# from the default env-file, so values here reach containers, not the YAML.
#
# Copy to .env.s3 and fill in. init.sh creates it with a random password if
# missing. Prefer `make s3-on` / `make s3-off` over editing by hand — they set
# both switches below together.

# ── Which services exist at all ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The MinIO services sit behind `profiles: ["s3"]` so they are not instantiated
# unless asked for: an unreachable image, a slow healthcheck or missing
# credentials must never be able to fail `make start` for someone who is not
# using this variant. testbed.sh passes this file as a second --env-file, and
# compose reads COMPOSE_PROFILES from it. Empty => MinIO does not run.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=

# ── The capability ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S3_ENABLED=1 makes the S3 path AVAILABLE: MinIO runs and the prepub entrypoint
# writes /etc/cvmfs/<repo>.s3.conf. It does NOT redirect anything by itself.
#
# Which path a publish takes is decided PER BUILD: prepub passes --direct-s3 to
# cvmfs_server when the job carries direct_s3=true (bits-console Build modal),
# and cvmfs_server reads its S3 settings from the config file above. The file's
# presence is not a switch — an early prototype worked that way, and building
# the testbed around it meant publishes went through the gateway while looking
# like they used S3.
#
# So leave this at 1 on a testbed used for comparing the two paths: turning it
# off means a build asking for direct_s3 fails instead of being comparable.
#
# NOTE: objects from a direct_s3 build land in MinIO, NOT under repos/<repo>
# where stratum0's Apache serves them, so a client cannot read them until the
# repository's data source is moved to MinIO too.
S3_ENABLED=0

# ── MinIO ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
S3_BUCKET=cvmfs
S3_HOST=minio
S3_PORT=9000
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_PARALLEL=16

MINIO_ROOT_USER=cvmfs-testbed
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=
